{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact d691e6e9d7511a5176cd9f827009762b7a62fa55. One P2 source finding remains in the malformed-content boundary. The integrity wording repair and four shipped decoder cases are credited below. This is the normal assigned source review of invitation a23cfe01368878719b3a1a73a12fda85c99246ba, my promise f6dd71f4807598abd6ce884b2eae865612fa6a4e, and only intermediate-release request 42342e35a7660b466b3f623309702461e8f44f6f / builder promise 4e66accc560de6f8ca320ee24593cb0df4f63448. Primary 8b9862104dd98b15a1f90affcc1138c1ac3c11d0 comes first; all 47 exact artifacts are bases. This verdict grants no source approval or landing.\n\nP2 — Check retained carry evidence before the direct read. packages/log/src/calls.ts:248 reads from.result.input.evidence.act before the try beginning at line 251. The retained-input decoder at packages/log/src/decode.ts:515-538 validates the context kind, input and budget objects, the optional proposal, changedSince and the land arrays, but it never validates the carry evidence object or its act field. CallSession.fromNext at calls.ts:168-177 accepts a decoded context with the matching carry kind. Consequently the dereference at 248 is not protected by the later catch or by the decoder's new consumed-field checks.\n\nThe public full-replay path reaches this method: verify.ts:1258-1259 calls checkCarry; its existing landing/version/evidence/configuration guards lead to an opened session and session.carry at verify.ts:978 when the checker has a pinned runner. verifyLog has no outer catch around this branch. The decoder's catch at verify.ts:474-478 protects decoding, which currently accepts this evidence shape, and cannot protect the later read. The ordinary recomputation path also calls the same carry method. This contradicts verify.ts:34-36's contract that malformed published content produces a named report failure and only repository reads can throw. A decoder that guards the other direct reads leaves this one exposed before digest comparison or semantic reconstruction can refuse it.\n\nRepair this specific boundary: require the carry evidence object and its string act field before consumption, or ensure that shape failure is converted to the existing named malformed report before that comparison. Preserve evidence identity comparison and full carry semantics. This asks for no universal retained-context schema, duplicate verifier, complete carry-pass implementation or broad validation sweep. Re-invite at the actual repaired exact head, with the original assigned binding and complete artifacts.\n\nConfidence is high in the source defect and its full-replay reachability. A new public runtime reproduction has not been executed, so this is explicitly a source-qualified finding. No integrity-mode exception is claimed for this carry branch: opts.replayDecisions:false takes the different branch at verify.ts:1253. No Room admission bypass, unauthorized publication, provider compromise or real-service denial has been demonstrated. No private probe is requested or required by this verdict.\n\nDelivered repairs credited. The prior 925790d7 wording finding is repaired. The machine cannotProve statements now name the checks integrity mode actually performs and distinguish them from policy replay. They accurately qualify the one-way comparison of available Git objects and a retained proposal context: omissions may use Git's list, extra paths are not refused by that comparison, the context-named base is not proven to be the merge base, and the complete context/budget are not rebuilt in integrity mode. Conditional admin-approval and ordinary rule obligations remain distinct. The CLI mode line, VerifyReport description, protocol and package guide agree. The complete execution suffix is unchanged; the decoder remains a changed execution dependency, so suffix identity does not establish unchanged behavior of the entire verifier.\n\nThe new decode boundary guards proposal base and changed-list elements, including rename.from; present carry changedSince strings; and land obligation.id/review.act objects. These are narrow guards using the existing decoder helpers. The complete four-path 342-to-d691 delta and ten-path 6b-to-d691 composition were read. The two Stage 5 client comment/test-variable clarifications are separately owned and outside this 47-artifact scope. The full f8-to-d691 composition contains eight paths; this is not disguised as only the four-path latest repair.\n\nRetained runtime evidence. I read and verified the previously completed ordinary shipped validation result; I did not rerun it. Its exact source is d691, Node26.10.0 and Vitest4.1.11. One Vitest process loaded 36 cases, selected the four unchanged shipped decoder cases, passed all four, skipped 32, failed none, and exited 0 in 0.926595084 seconds. Exact argv/cwd and the six-field sanitized environment, stdout/stderr, complete result, source archive, before/after identities and restoration are retained at /tmp/artroom-checker-verifier-d691-runtime-u07yw4am. All 15 evidence-file seals match, and all 738 tracked fixture paths still match their exact Git objects.\n\nThose four cases pair an unchanged signed fixture prefix with the malformed retained content at the same selected entry. Their honest controls pass full and integrity modes. The shipped full-mode assertions require malformed at proposal entry17 or land entry23, with verifiedThrough16 or22 respectively. Integrity asserts a failed malformed report and matching detail, without asserting the full-mode prefix boundary. The tests emit no separate raw VerifyReport, retained-content digest listing, generated publication or passive reader log; none is claimed as saved runtime evidence. They use synthetic room-signed offline fixtures and prove nothing about real Room admission. They do not cover the remaining carry-evidence direct read. The producer's four old-decoder controls, other301 log tests and 2053-test integrated gate remain attributed producer results, not newly executed checker results.\n\nArchitecture. The consumed-field validation belongs at the existing decoding/report boundary, before any shape-dependent read. Preserve semantic reconstruction and exact digest comparison as separate checks. The repaired wording makes the delivered bounded verifier useful without presenting integrity as full replay or partial carry accounting as complete. The new finding is a small boundary omission within that design; it does not justify a new engine or extending this intermediate request into full Stage3.\n\nSecurity. This review concerns robustness of the offline consumer of retained publication content and the truth of its report. The four delivered cases are repaired and independently supported by the retained result. The remaining direct read crosses the promised malformed-report boundary in full replay. Existing authority, actor/binding, step-version and honest unsupported behavior remain part of the complete sealed scope; the prior useful legacy/decoder witnesses transfer only where exact source/dependency identities permit. No credential, provider or deployment action occurred in this review.\n\nSimplification. Keep one field-specific validation boundary, the existing helpers, truthful public limits and compact useful witnesses. No broad gate was rerun merely to finish this source review. No added MCP test quota, extra Jam gate or blanket complete-schema claim follows from it. Preserve the 10x useful-invariant test economy and measure the actual future integrated composition under its owner.\n\nIndependent identity and evidence checks. All 47 current artifact raw commits were independently read: payload head/path match; immutable raw bases match the public bases and name only builder promise4e66accc; source byte lengths, SHA-256 and Git blob identities match. All 47 remain effective, exact d691 and non-stale in fresh authoritative inspection at depths15580-15585. The primary-first list is canonical. Artifact event trees contain only event; source archives/copies are separate owned evidence, not event attachments. All 942 retained source-evidence seals match. Both retained source and runtime copies of all 738 tracked files/symlinks independently hash to the exact Git tree; no mismatch or source/test change was found. The registered review checkout is clean and at d691. Checks are retained in root-artifact-checks.json and root-retained-evidence-checks.json beside this verdict.\n\nScope and current direction. The normal prepare binds this delivery only to42342e35 and explicitly excludes original Stage3 completion. Stage3 request1e8fee4b/promise3af8ebc7 and Stage4 request48c021ea/promise8d497ff5 remain owed until their own proper dispositions. This review does not close complete carry accounting, the whole original Stage3/4 scope, all fifteen cases of adopted015, the original ten and A-F, prepared/consumer-before-producer consistency, Stage6 transitions, UI C5, original intent retention, public starter/manual or the MCP runtime/core conditions. Existing Stage2, bearer, Stage5 and packaging approvals retain their exact historical subjects. The withdrawn25bede37 approval is not revived. The final matching packages, integrated candidate and normal redeployment remain separate source/release/effect work.\n\nI read current sprint direction c514748f and decision5c020815: the integration branch is frozen at d691, the whole head cannot land until both verifier and MCP approvals, and a changes-requested verdict requires a repaired head and re-invitation. MCP branch7f65de2c is separately filed and differs in its delivery ledger; its two original scopes still require their own binding/review. Current R0 verdict92abd211 is an evidence-only design-adoption input. Its cancellation ledger remains proposed, makes no closure, and does not nullify the current sprint decision. The d4e07064 demo-first/composable/all-component-removal direction still governs successor work. No source change or landing is performed by this verdict, and no schedule narrows functional acceptance.\n\nRestricted-action boundary. The same existing checker task was resumed by the user, with current read-only execution independently observed active and error null in20ce53a3. The earlier automated cybersecurity rejection of a private diagnostic remains recorded. No rejected private diagnostic was rerun, rewritten, extended, delegated, or used as fresh d691 execution; no reviewer/task/model/backend was replaced or switched. This turn used static exact-source/provenance reads and existing retained evidence only. The earlier completed private342 diagnostic is neither a current reproduction nor the basis for a claimed runtime outcome here. This source verdict is not a guard override or evidence-only source approval.\n\nDisposition: changes requested for the one source-qualified P2 carry-evidence boundary omission. Credit the delivered repairs and qualified retained test evidence. The builder can make the bounded repair and file the next exact normal invitation; all still-open original and successor obligations retain their owners.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8b9862104dd98b15a1f90affcc1138c1ac3c11d0","binding":"assigned","head":"d691e6e9d7511a5176cd9f827009762b7a62fa55","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e53f7c64a085a0681ac1871fc91e4ca7d78bf2b9\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:56407f106646fc44539c4c79682e59b4588efbb5\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f6dd71f4807598abd6ce884b2eae865612fa6a4e\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aabbeaa8489aecded8b15c0e9285a8c933c77534\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bbc5a412de67dae13fc70604ce4462409a3c9883\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25c25dc3f2da57ceae68506edf65e161e273